Subject: [PATCH] wmediumd: admit queued frames per transmitter frequency

Reserve only the head of each transmitter/frequency FIFO, instead of allowing
an entire sender backlog to reserve future medium time and precompute stale
receive eligibility. Preserve kernel arrival order across access categories,
independent frequency operation on multi-channel hwsim PHYs, packet rates,
retry counts, contention windows, airtime accounting and directed visibility.
Account pending frames from ingress, retain original client ownership and
cancel active and pending jobs when their client disconnects.

Self-tests cover a 32-frame backlog, bounded peer admission, same-PHY
frequency independence, FIFO across categories, deferred receive eligibility,
and removal of active/pending frames with mixed client ownership. Run those
cases with both global contention and opt-in visibility reservations.

